      "title": { "en": "The plural of mówić" },
      "body": { "en": "*Mówimy*, *mówicie*, *mówią*: again *-my* for \"we\", *-cie* for \"you\" and *-ą* for \"they\". You now know three verbs in full: *być*, *mieć* and *mówić*." },
      "conjugation": {
        "verb": "mówić",
        "meaning": { "en": "to speak" },
        "forms": { "ja": "mówię", "ty": "mówisz", "on": "mówi", "my": "mówimy", "wy": "mówicie", "oni": "mówią" }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a1-u02-d08-t02",
      "before": "a1-u02-d08-e07",
      "title": { "en": "Polakiem, Polką" },
      "body": { "en": "After *jestem*, *jesteś* and *jest*, the word for what someone is takes a special ending. A man says *jestem Polakiem* or *jestem Anglikiem*, a woman *jestem Polką* or *jestem Angielką*. Unit 4 explains this ending; a name does not change (*jestem Adam*). If your country is not here, *jestem z…* always works." }
    }
  ],
